  "jobTitle": "Web Developer",
  "summary": "I’m a web designer and developer with Cengage Learning, a publisher of college textbooks and online products and services including textbook companion sites, instructor and student online resources, and electronic books.\n\nWith nearly 8 years of experience, I have a broad skill set in web design and development that I use to create the best possible web-based products for Cengage Learning. Sometimes it’s in the design and layout phase while other times it is in building the code. Either way, I delight in creating sites that are clean, using modern web standards, with strong usability and cross-browser compatibility. I also ensure that the sites are accessible to all users, such as those visually impaired utilizing screen readers. I work closely with all project stakeholders (marketing, designers, back-end developers, etc.) who often have competing interests. I’ve developed skills in all the areas involved in order to bridge the knowledge gap among the stakeholders and I often serve as mediator to resolve conflicts.  \n\nI am the go-to person for troubleshooting issues around cross-browser compatibility and accessibility. I work daily in Sublime Text (for coding), JQuery, Firebug, and Photoshop. I am a strong believer in open source software. I setup my personal computer with Linux (Ubuntu Studio) running Firefox, GIMP, Inkscape, etc. I like learning new things and exploring new ideas and ways of doing things that push my limits.  And, I like to have a really good time in the process!\n\nPrior to starting my career in web design and development I was an independent studio artist, making and selling art pottery and sculpture. I taught classes, workshops, and private lessons on ceramics. I was the lead of a major community wood-fired kiln construction and firing project.\n\nI’m always interested in hearing from former and current colleagues, others working in web development, artistic types, and creative individuals, so please contact me if you’d like to connect.",
